  "result": "Excellent! I've successfully implemented the voucher functionality. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**Updated: `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: \"Only one voucher per invoice.\"\n\n**Updated: `src/invoices.js`**\n- Modified `invoiceTotals()` to:\n  - Accept invoices with optional `voucher` property\n  - Return `voucher` field in the totals object (0 if none applied)\n  - Calculate total as: `subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n  - Clamp total to 0 if voucher exceeds the total\n\n- Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function:\n  - Validates invoice status is 'draft' (returns NOT_DRAFT otherwise)\n  - Prevents multiple vouchers per invoice (returns VOUCHER_EXISTS if one exists)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (returns AMOUNT_INVALID otherwise)\n  - Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n  - Returns non-mutated new invoice object\n\n**Updated: `test/invoices.test.js`**\n- Updated all 11 existing `invoiceTotals` tests to include `voucher: 0` in expected results\n- Added 14 comprehensive voucher tests covering:\n  - Basic voucher application\n  - Error handling (NOT_DRAFT, VOUCHER_EXISTS, AMOUNT_INVALID)\n  - Voucher in calculations (applied after VAT, before total clamping)\n  - Edge cases (large amounts, total clamping, field preservation)\n  - Integration with terms and discounts\n\n**Test Results**: All 162 tests pass (148 existing + 14 new)\n\nThe implementation correctly applies vouchers as a fixed discount after VAT calculation, prevents duplicate vouchers, and integrates seamlessly with all existing invoice features.",
